{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/990997-m20-is-it-possible-to-afford-a-familiar-without-prime-or-constant-access-to-a-node","id":990997,"title":"[M20] Is it possible to afford a Familiar without Prime or constant access to a Node?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-21T09:45:53-07:00","id":990997,"title":"[M20] Is it possible to afford a Familiar without Prime or constant access to a Node?","content":"Going through M20 I encountered the Familiar background (p.314-316). I kinda like it, but then I realized that you need constant access to a steady stream of Quintessence. If you don't have a Node or dots in Prime you're severely limited in how much Quintessence you can obtain, meaning that if you want a somewhat powerful Familiar (3 and more dots) you're going to be constantly working to obtain the stuff. So how would you go about gathering the Quintessence in such a case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T10:12:30-07:00","id":991008,"title":"","content":"Make deals with the Nephandi. Anything so that the Familiar is certain to have food in his bowl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T11:00:22-07:00","id":991035,"title":"","content":"Hearts Blood, your familiar slowly devours you...<br /> Nevermind, that requires Prime at 1.<br /> <br /> I agree with you, that mage works constantly to earn tass. Great for the ST to involve you in any plot he wants...\ud83d\udc7f","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T17:16:32-07:00","id":991184,"title":"","content":"According to <i>Forged By Dragon's Fire</i>, certain Familiars have the Quintessence Grazing Charm, which allows them to gather Quintessence on their own. It's limited to one Quintessence per day if the Familiar has access to a Node, or one Quint per week otherwise. So a 1 dot Familiar can take care of itself (although, it also needs to spend most of its time looking for fractions of Quintessence points), but a 3 dot Familiar still requires help. Still, it's better than nothing.<br /> <br /> Now, Quintessence Grazing is an expensive Charm to buy at the Familiar's character creation (7 freebie points). But Bygone and Elemental Familiars have this Charm for free (to make up for the fact that they give their pact partner Paradox every time they are seen by Sleepers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T18:23:18-07:00","id":991202,"title":"","content":"Not having Prime is pretty rough.<br /> <br /> Though if you really want to avoid having dots in Prime, you can use Wonders instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T01:23:29-07:00","id":991306,"title":"","content":"Periapts are a possibility.<br /> A Bloodfire Ruby can recharge its storage by being submersed over night in a bucket of blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T02:19:44-07:00","id":991315,"title":"","content":"According to Mage20 you need Prime 2 to draw Quintessence from a Periapt, plus you need to charge it too (p.632), so that's not an option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/990997-m20-is-it-possible-to-afford-a-familiar-without-prime-or-constant-access-to-a-node?p=991184#post991184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, Quintessence Grazing is an expensive Charm to buy at the Familiar's character creation (7 freebie points).</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean that you roll up stats for the Familiar itself, or that this is something the Mage must buy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T02:34:42-07:00","id":991317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/990997-m20-is-it-possible-to-afford-a-familiar-without-prime-or-constant-access-to-a-node?p=991315#post991315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean that you roll up stats for the Familiar itself, or that this is something the Mage must buy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both.<br /> <br /> At the PC's character creation, when you buy dots in the Familiar Background, you also do character creation for the Familiar. In addition to the base dots to be distributed for that Familiar, each dot in the Background gives you 10 freebie points to spend on improving them. It's those freebie points that go towards buying Familiar Charms, which can include Quintessence Grazing (unless it's a Bygone or Elemental type Familiar, who get the Charm for free).<br /> <br /> That's for character creation. After that, the Familiar behaves like a regular character, including the ability to improve with experience points. But it's the Mage that has to spend their exp to improve their pact partner, which can include buying new Charms. This can be problematic for players who have characters with Familiars, since they need to split their experience points between their own advancement and that of their partner. A Storyteller might alleviate this a bit by giving exp that can only be used by the Familiar, but that's neither here nor there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T02:35:55-07:00","id":991319,"title":"","content":"Make a combo Talisman/Periapt that has Prime 2 for channeling, and extra quint storage; so that's still on the table.<br /> <br /> The Quintessence Grazing Charm is part of the expanded Revised Familiar rules that involve stating up the Familiar more fully. It's probably going to be covered in the Book of Secrets when it comes out for M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T03:10:30-07:00","id":991321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/990997-m20-is-it-possible-to-afford-a-familiar-without-prime-or-constant-access-to-a-node?p=991315#post991315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to Mage20 you need Prime 2 to draw Quintessence from a Periapt, plus you need to charge it too (p.632), so that's not an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>A periapt in contact with you can be accessed without Prime, but in this case you don't want the quint, but your familiar.<br /> You can of course draw upon a periapt in LOS with Prime, and you can charge it with Prime. Neither of those statements rules out that a familiar and a periapt can function without a mage with Prime.<br /> <br /> Edit: In my M20 book page 632 refers to Spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":". 10-22-2016, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T04:13:19-07:00","id":991331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/990997-m20-is-it-possible-to-afford-a-familiar-without-prime-or-constant-access-to-a-node?p=991317#post991317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both.<br /> <br /> At the PC's character creation, when you buy dots in the Familiar Background, you also do character creation for the Familiar. In addition to the base dots to be distributed for that Familiar, each dot in the Background gives you 10 freebie points to spend on improving them. It's those freebie points that go towards buying Familiar Charms, which can include Quintessence Grazing (unless it's a Bygone or Elemental type Familiar, who get the Charm for free).<br /> <br /> That's for character creation. After that, the Familiar behaves like a regular character, including the ability to improve with experience points. But it's the Mage that has to spend their exp to improve their pact partner, which can include buying new Charms. This can be problematic for players who have characters with Familiars, since they need to split their experience points between their own advancement and that of their partner. A Storyteller might alleviate this a bit by giving exp that can only be used by the Familiar, but that's neither here nor there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are yougetting all this from? M20 suggests that this information is going to be in <i>Gods, Monsters, and Other Familiar Strangers</i>, which is a stretch goal book that's under no threat of coming out any time soon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/990997-m20-is-it-possible-to-afford-a-familiar-without-prime-or-constant-access-to-a-node?p=991321#post991321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: In my M20 book page 632 refers to Spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops, meant 652.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T05:04:39-07:00","id":991344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/990997-m20-is-it-possible-to-afford-a-familiar-without-prime-or-constant-access-to-a-node?p=991331#post991331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are yougetting all this from? M20 suggests that this information is going to be in <i>Gods, Monsters, and Other Familiar Strangers</i>, which is a stretch goal book that's under no threat of coming out any time soon.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Forged By Dragon's Fire</i>, a Revised era book published near the tail end of the old World of Darkness. It's mostly about Wonders, but the last chapter has extensive rules about Familiars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T06:39:54-07:00","id":991369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/990997-m20-is-it-possible-to-afford-a-familiar-without-prime-or-constant-access-to-a-node?p=991331#post991331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whoops, meant 652.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, in HDYDT it is described as it was in revised.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HDYDT p.45</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Accessing Tass or Periapt Quintessence</b><br /> Under normal circumstances, a mage with Tass, a Periapt, or a Matrix on his person can access that battery\u2019s Quintessence reflexively \u2013 that is, without using an additional Effect. If that battery is within reach but not touching the character, he can use a Prime 2 Effect to get the energy. And if the battery is some distance away, he can use Correspondence 2/ Prime 2 in order to draw upon the energy within the Periapt.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T07:02:38-07:00","id":991377,"title":"","content":"Ah, so you just gotta hold it.<br /> <br /> Hm, but you still have to charge it somehow though and that Quintessence has to come from somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T16:00:14-07:00","id":991571,"title":"","content":"So you would have to depend on the generosity of other Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:12:03-07:00","id":991610,"title":"","content":"<i>How Do You Do That?</i> is an interesting case, since it's information deviates wildly from other books, both pre- and post-M20. This not even mentioning the differences between all the editions collectively. Take everything with a grain of salt, and choose the option you like best is my motto. Golden Rule, y'all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T00:47:30-07:00","id":991766,"title":"","content":"Another option would be to give the familiar the legend background (preM20 this was possible), the<br /> downside is that the quint supply is not part of the pact. Quite possibly you are required to make it worthwhile for the familiar some other way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T06:01:54-07:00","id":1122674,"title":"","content":"(a bit of a necro i know but...) The v20quickstart has a character whose familiar is a spirit crow made manifest and the character just feed it bit of expensive and rare morsels of food and apparently that passes for quintessence, do you think this could be an option ? Acquiring rare and exotic materials or food to feed your familiar with it so it can have its quintessence for the week ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T08:57:35-07:00","id":1122716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/990997-m20-is-it-possible-to-afford-a-familiar-without-prime-or-constant-access-to-a-node?p=1122674#post1122674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(a bit of a necro i know but...) The v20quickstart has a character whose familiar is a spirit crow made manifest and the character just feed it bit of expensive and rare morsels of food and apparently that passes for quintessence, do you think this could be an option ? Acquiring rare and exotic materials or food to feed your familiar with it so it can have its quintessence for the week ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Feed it Tass? Or just weird stuff in accordance with the deal made? <br /> <br /> E.g. In Mage fiction, Penny Dreadful the Hollow One steals the Nephandus Jodi Blake's sp.?) Familiar by offering it tastier and less grotesque meals, among other perks. At no time in the stories does she seem to be doing something that indicates she's forking over Quintessence, though maybe that's just how her Focus (though that term is meaningless in the context of such an Old School Mage character) handles Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T01:23:31-07:00","id":1123356,"title":"","content":"In FbDF in the Introductionary tale in the chapter on Familiars she clearly expends quint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}